0678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,50,70206,57960,9407,220,16,15,24884,43298,1124,9407,220,18,15,24884,43298,1124,9407,220,20,15,24884,43298,1124,9407,220,22,15,24884,43298,2418,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nSimplify $\\cos 10^\\circ \\cos 30^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ \\cos 70^\\circ.$","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"2af3602d76c3376f3ee7bcf9a054d2c1d4481e4955dede0878b3c472bbe40c36"},"seconds":26.743826866149902,"seed":798842323194284668,"stop":"eos","text":"To simplify the expression $\\cos 10^\\circ \\cos 30^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ \\cos 70^\\circ$, we'll use trigonometric identities and properties. The problem can be approached by using the product-to-sum identities and the known values of trigonometric functions at specific angles.\n\nFirst, let's recall that $\\cos 30^\\circ = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$. We can then rewrite the expression as:\n\n\\[\n\\cos 10^\\circ \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\cdot \\cos 50^\\circ \\cdot \\cos 70^\\circ.\n\\]\n\nTo simplify the product $\\cos 10^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ \\cos 70^\\circ$, we use the identity for the product of cosines. One useful identity is:\n\n\\[\n\\cos x \\cos (60^\\circ - x) \\cos (60^\\circ + x) = \\frac{1}{4} \\cos 3x.\n\\]\n\nHere, we set $x = 10^\\circ$. Then, $\\cos 10^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ \\cos 70^\\circ = \\frac{1}{4} \\cos (3 \\cdot 10^\\circ) = \\frac{1}{4} \\cos 30^\\circ = \\frac{1}{4} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{8}$.\n\nNow, substituting this back into our original expression, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\cos 10^\\circ \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\cdot \\cos 50^\\circ \\cdot \\cos 70^\\circ = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{8} = \\frac{3}{16}.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the simplified expression is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{3}{16}}.\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{\\frac{3}{16}}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
